-- FINDING 5, companion (silent).  The only way to put the Gazette's 5.00 pm into a gate is to compare NOW with a
-- DATETIME.  But the reading-day pin is a DATE (00:00 UTC, which is 08:00 in Singapore), so a reader pinned to
-- 31 October 2012 reads at 08:00, before 5.00 pm, and the NOW gate answers "not yet published" for the whole
-- of that day, whatever hour the real reader read.  The DATE gate (TODAY AT LEAST 31 Oct 2012) says "published".
-- Neither is right for every reader on the day; the language cannot hold the within-day split.
--
-- Printed: first line FALSE (NOW gate, 31 Oct 2012), second TRUE (NOW gate, 1 Nov 2012), third TRUE (DATE gate).
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT datetime
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

`the Gazette instant` MEANS Datetime (Date 31 10 2012) 17 0 0

`published, by NOW` MEANS NOW AT LEAST `the Gazette instant`
`published, by TODAY` MEANS TODAY AT LEAST (Date 31 10 2012)

#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 31 10 2012) `published, by NOW`
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 11 2012) `published, by NOW`
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 31 10 2012) `published, by TODAY`
